      "message": "Hi Bart,\nOn boot `blk_mq_alloc_sched_res()` in `block/blk-mq-sched.c` calls `blk_mq_default_nr_requests(set)` (in `block/blk-mq.h`), which still returns `2 * queue_depth`.\n This means `q-\u003enr_requests` will default to `2 * queue_depth` at startup before any sysfs write occurs, leaving the ZWOR deadlock open on boot. Should `blk_mq_alloc_sched_res()` (or `blk_mq_default_nr_requests()`) also check `blk_use_zwor(q)` so that initial scheduler tags are capped at `1 * queue_depth` on boot?",
